    {
      "id": "c90e774345077e1696213d39f1d3fc08e65943b8",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 777608666,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I don't know how to fix the Win32/Win64 image build. I can't reproduce it.\n\nWe should probably add a check for the minimum MSVC+SDK versions but I'm not sure how to do that either.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jvalverde"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-12-15T15:03:00.247Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-12-15T18:31:38.880Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 131025187,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 5443,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 778097515,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "It looks like it's the SDK version. The MR builder has 10.0.19041.0 installed and the package builders had 10.0.17763.0 installed. I upgraded the package builders to 10.0.19041.0, then to 10.0.22000.0.\n\n10.0.17763.0: Fails with a syntax error, which means there's no `/wdxxxx` workaround.\\\n10.0.18362.0: OK with `/wd5105` according to your comment in CMakeLists.txt.\\\n10.0.19041.0: OK with `/wd5105`, tested locally.\\\n10.0.19041.685: Untested.\\\n10.0.20348.0: Untested.\\\n10.0.22000.0: `/wd5105` not needed.\\\n\nCMake prints version information at the beginning of its output if the SDK and target version are different, e.g. \"Selecting Windows SDK version 10.0.19041.0 to target Windows 10.0.17763.\" It looks like the SDK version is exposed as CMAKE_VS_WINDOWS_TARGET_PLATFORM_VERSION.",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1789948913",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-12-15T18:31:38.812Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-12-15T18:31:38.812Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 131025187,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 5443,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 778123694,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "SDK 10.0.18362.0 is the minimum required version so the builders should be good now.\n\nI will investigate using CMAKE_VS_WINDOWS_TARGET_PLATFORM_VERSION to check for this.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
